(D1b — Discrepancy 1, in the exact shape the generator already emits.
 `src/gen_misc.vox:383` emits a flag-reader function, and
 `src/gen_core.vox:963` rotates six prelude blocks so that the reader can
 be emitted BEFORE the flag schema it reads — deliberately, and the
 comment at `src/gen_misc.vox:369-375` records that this was hand-verified
 as legal Vox. It is legal. On 0.4.9 and earlier it was also one line away
 from printing a pointer.
 The reader as emitted survived only because it copied the text flag into
 a DECLARED text local first (`a text called fl1local is fl1label.`) and
 printed the local. This probe is that function with the copy removed —
 `Print fl1label.` straight from the forward-referenced global. Run with
 no arguments so the flag takes its declared default `"d1"`.
 Same defect as D1.vox, reached through the generator's own prelude rather
 than a hand-written example.
 RESOLVED, 2026-08-22 — vox #66, same fix as D1.vox. Re-run verbatim
 against 0.4.10: the in-function read now prints `d1`, matching the
 top-level read, where 0.4.9 printed a stack address that varied per run
 (which is why this probe still asserts on EXIT CODE as well: it exits 3
 unconditionally either way).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D1b.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   d1
   d1
   exit 3
)
To 'read flags 1'.
    Print fl1label.

a flag called fl1label is "-a" or "--alpha1", it is a text with default "d1".
Parse flags.

Print fl1label.
'read flags 1'.
Exit 3.
